NAME
       sh - POSIX-style shell

SYNOPSIS
       sh [-c command] [script]

DESCRIPTION
       A smaller shell kept for scripts that expect POSIX syntax. For
       interactive work csh(1) is the better choice.

OPTIONS
       -c C   run C and exit
       -n     read without executing
       -v     echo input lines as they are read

SEE ALSO
       csh(1), test(1)
